# Devin .knowledge bridge

Use the repository-root `AGENTS.md` as the primary `.knowledge` instruction
contract. This separate Devin rule is only a concise vendor-specific discovery
bridge; it must not duplicate or override the shared managed block.

For meaningful scoped work, run `node .knowledge/tools/agent-task.js begin`
before broad exploration, read the exact returned first-read body, and finish
with `node .knowledge/tools/agent-task.js finish` using the returned workflow ID,
first-read SHA, physical source files, and physical test argv. The committed
result keeps primary verification, routing, Doctor, Task Readiness, native repair
receipts, optional release warnings, and deferred debt separate.

Never describe the deterministic local first-read estimate as provider-reported
model-token usage, cost, speed, or general accuracy.

For concurrent work, set a stable `KNOWLEDGE_AGENT_ID` and use a separate
worktree or branch.

If a meaningful task or required `.knowledge` write is blocked, do not silently
skip it. Use `node .knowledge/tools/recording-blockers.js list` when available
and relay its `chat_notice` in the user's preferred language, naming the
blocked item and reason. Mask secret values. Obey a user boundary that excludes
`.knowledge/`; leave the blocker visibly `blocked_by_user_scope` and never
bypass the scope. Say: “Если это не секрет, сообщите в чате или выберите
действие в Inspector”. This instruction is not a mechanical guarantee for
every runner.
